[DOORREPO CONFIGURATION FILE]

This file configures the DoorRepo door client. Copy this file to your door configuration
directory and customize the settings for your BBS. All settings are optional; if a setting
is omitted, a safe default is used.

RepoHost=bbs.uprough.net
The hostname or IP address of the door repository server. Default: bbs.uprough.net

RepoPort=80
The TCP port number for the repository server connection. Default: 80

RepoPath=/api/door-repo
The HTTP path prefix for the repository API endpoints. Default: /api/door-repo

DownloadDir=T:
The AmigaDOS directory where downloaded door archives are saved. Must exist before
use. Default: T: (temporary directory)

PageSize=20
The number of doors to display per page when browsing the repository. Default: 20

TimeoutSecs=30
The maximum number of seconds to wait for a response from the repository server.
Default: 30

LhaCommand=lha
The name or full path of the LHA archive extraction utility, used if ExtractAfterDownload
is enabled. Default: lha

ExtractAfterDownload=no
Whether to automatically extract downloaded archives. Set to yes, no, 1, or 0.
Default: no

LogFile=T:DoorRepo.log
The AmigaDOS path where the door logs its activity and errors. Default: T:DoorRepo.log

[EXAMPLES]

All defaults (line everything out to use them):
[commented out: all keys]

Faster network, local extraction:
RepoHost=10.0.0.50
RepoPort=8080
TimeoutSecs=60
ExtractAfterDownload=yes
DownloadDir=RAM:

[NOTES]

- Case does not matter for key names (RepoHost, repohost, REPOHOST all work)
- Leading and trailing whitespace around keys and values is ignored
- Lines starting with # are comments and are ignored
- Empty lines are ignored
- Unknown keys are silently skipped
